'''Little Oka''' ({{lang-bl|Piqueño Oka}}; {{Langx|ok|努雅羅緒華|Nuugara Oka}}), alternatively known as '''Okataian Quarter''' ({{Lang-bl|Barrio Okano}}), is a barrio of the [[Limón|Limón borough]] of [[Castejón]]. It is the oldest [[W:Ethnic enclave|ethnic enclave]] in [[Balisca]] and the largest [[Oka|Okataian]] [[W:ethnic enclave|enclave]] outside [[W:Asia|Asia]]. It is also one of the largest of the [[Ethnic enclaves in Balisca|over twenty ethnic enclaves within Castejón]]. 

Despite facing numerous attempts at gentrification, Little Oka remains a vibrant enclave that continues to retain its own customs, [[Okataian|dialects]], places of worship, social clubs, and identity.

